  "tool_boundary": "Host/glibc original AOSP checkpolicy/checkmodule, static libsepol. No host runtime injected. Source libsepol3.7, upstream refpolicy declares3.9+; tested MCS/systemd/format30 passes but full supported-toolchain matrix remains unproved. Generated policy_parse.h from original grammar required by original lexer; source unchanged.",
  "limits": "AOSP baseline is original GSI platform CIL only, not full vendor/hardware policy; Linux baseline full selected default modules. Different scope must not imply equal host/device coverage. Merely differing class/permission order is not a proved ABI failure; mappings need evaluation. Shared literal attributes are a collision risk, not a demonstrated access leak.",
  "negative_control": "Both original CIL inputs in global namespace fail role object_r redeclaration, despite -m; no neverallow bypass. This rejects only naive unmodified composition, not either adapted strategy.",
  "rejected_inventory": "First own access-vector regex omitted inherited classes without explicit braces (74/136). Never accepted; retained local. Corrected token parser verifies every security_classes declaration and all136 permission lists/orders against independent original compiler CIL.",
